  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing the town of East Hampton to alienate and convey certain\nparcels of land used as parkland for the purpose of a Suffolk County roadway\nimprovement project",
    "basePrintNo": "S9741",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9741-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Parks",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9741\n\nSPONSOR: PALUMBO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act authorizing the town of East Hampton to alienate and convey\ncertain parcels of land used as parkland for the purpose of a Suffolk\nCounty roadway improvement project\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAuthorizes the Town of East Hampton to alienate and convey certain\nparcels of land used as parkland for the purpose of a Suffolk County\nroadway improvement projects\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Authorizes the Town of East Hampton to discontinue as park-\nland a parcel located at the intersection of Three Mile Harbor Road and\nSprings Fireplace Road and convey it to the Suffolk County for the\npurposes of a roadway improvement project.\n\nSection 2. Provides that authorization to discontinue said parkland\nshall only be effective on the condition that the Town of East Hampton\nacquire and dedicate a parcel of land located at located at 16 Swamp\nRoad as parkland, provided the Town has never used such lands for public\nopen space or park purposes.\n\nSection 3. Describes the metes and bounds of the parklands to be alien-\nated\n\nSection 4. Describes the metes and bounds of the parcel that shall be\nacquired and dedicated as parklands\n\nSection 5. Section regarding the fair market value of the lands being\ndiscontinued and the lands to be acquired.\n\nSection 6. States that if the Town of East Hampton received any funding\nsupport or assistance from the federal government for the purchase,\nmaintenance, or improvement of the parklands set forth in\n\nSection 3 of this act, the discontinuance and alienation of such park-\nland authorized by the provisions of this act cannot occur until the\nTown of East Hampton complied with any federal requirements related to\nthe alienation or conversion of parklands, including satisfying the\nSecretary of the Interior deems necessary to assure the substitution of\nother lands shall be the equivalent in fair market value and usefulness\nto the lands being alienated or converted.\n\nSection 7. Sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nSuffolk County will be undertaking a roadway improvement project for CR\n40 (a.k.a Three Mile Harbor Road) from Collins Avenue to Copeces Lane.\nThere is a point on CR40 that intersects with CR 41 (Springs Fireplace\nRoad). This location routinely experiences traffic delays and congestion\nfor vehicles that are southbound on CR 41 and need to cross over to CR\n40. In addition, traffic will back up on CR 40 southbound while cars are\ncrossing over from CR 41. As such, the Town of East Hampton is support-\nive of the project including a roundabout at the intersection of CR 40\nand CR 41.\n\nThe Suffolk County Department of Public Works recently conducted a\npublic information session to present its conceptual project plans.\nWhile the proposed plans currently do not recommend including a rounda-\nbout, the County did not rule it out as a possibility to address traffic\nflow issues at this intersection. One of the issues, however, is that\nthe land that would be needed to construct a roundabout is designated\nparkland.\n\nAccordingly, the Town of East Hampton has requested the introduction of\nthis legislation which is necessary to enable the alienation of the\nparkland at this location (SCTM  300-163-3-7) and swap it for a compara-\nble parcel of land located at 16 Swamp Road (STM  300-133-2-6.2) for the\npurposes of constructing a roundabout.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2024: New Legislation\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
